{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold on this record, so the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is legitimately chargeable. Limb (a): EV-TRIP-02760 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 12:28:24 (driver tapped 'I'm Here'). Limb (b): EV-GPS-02760 places the driver inside the pickup geofence from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 12:28:24. Limb (c): the in-geofence dwell runs continuously for 482 seconds from 12:28:24 to 12:36:26 against a free waiting period of 180 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold applies). Limb (d): the trip was terminated by the driver at 12:36:26 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after that dwell had elapsed. EV-GPS-02760 is impaired at weight 0.85, issue GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW, a single 60-second pre-wait gap that does not touch the arrival or the dwell run.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02760", "EV-GPS-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-02 arrival test is satisfied with room to spare. EV-GPS-02760 records qualifying_fix_count = 49 in-radius fixes at the STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m, on a 10-second sampled trace, far more than the 3 consecutive in-radius fixes the clause requires. EV-GPS-02760 is impaired at 0.85 (GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW), and I disclose that; the impairment is a 60-second gap at 12:25:04-12:26:04, before the arrival marker, and so does not touch any of the 49 qualifying fixes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 does not govern this trip. That clause applies only where the driver's stationary fixes lie OUTSIDE the POL-NS-02 arrival radius (but within 400 m of the pin). Here the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m radius, so the wrong-entrance route is not engaged and the ordinary no-show analysis under POL-NS-01 applies. (EV-GPS-02760, impaired at 0.85, GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW — a gap outside the arrival window that leaves the in-radius run intact.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker was TRUE, so POL-NS-05 finds nothing to correct. The 'arrived' event at 12:28:24 coincides with the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 12:28:24 (derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec = 0.0), and the driver's fixes show a held position (speed 0.0 kph) rather than motion at or above the 15 kph POL-NS-05 threshold and far inside the 300 m test. The waiting clock therefore starts from the arrival event itself. (EV-GPS-02760 impaired at 0.85, GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW; the gap is outside the waiting window and does not affect this pairing.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall, so the POL-NS-06 refund route cannot operate. The effective in-geofence dwell is 482 seconds against a required 180 seconds, a surplus of 302 seconds (derived.arrival.shortfall_sec = -302.0). POL-NS-06 refunds only where the dwell is SHORTER than the free waiting period; it is not. (EV-GPS-02760 impaired at 0.85, issue GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW, a short gap outside the waiting window that does not shorten the measured run.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own words are 'I was there', but the rider's own track says otherwise. EV-GPS-02760's rider_presence block places every one of the rider's 87 fixes at approximately 806 to 814 m from the pickup pin, with rider_qualifying_fix_count = 0 — never once inside the 100 m STANDARD rider_presence_radius_m. The rider was roughly eight hundred metres from the pickup point throughout the waiting window. The rider track is carried by the same artifact, impaired at 0.85 under GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW, which I disclose.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider because limb (a) fails outright. EV-CHAT-02760 holds exactly one message and it is the driver's — 'hi im at the pickup point', sent 12:28:49 and read by the rider at 12:29:29. There is no rider message during the waiting window, so there is no locating or coordinating message to trigger the rider-contact exoneration, and the failure of limb (a) disposes of the clause without reaching limb (b) or (c).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"]
    },
    {
      "text": "With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force — SGD 3.60 (EV-FARE-02760 derived money.driver_compensation = '3.60', driver_compensation_rate 0.8) — the residual 20 percent being retained as the platform service fee. The driver drove to the pin, held position for the full free period and beyond, and is entitled to that compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, so the SGD 3.60 compensation must be paid rather than withheld. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, well below the threshold of 4 that the clause requires as the first limb; the absolute-count limb alone fails, and no rate computation can rescue it. Only the two fields the clause names (no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d) may be used for this check.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d"
    },
    {
      "text": "The charge itself reconciles, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect and no arithmetic basis for any refund. EV-FARE-02760 shows cancellation_fee SGD 4.50, matching trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0. Under POL-GEN-03 the filing rider's claim is unsupported and the present state — the charge standing — is left exactly as it is.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02760", "EV-TRIP-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged"
    },
    {
      "text": "The missing traffic advisory costs this case nothing. EV-ADVIS-02760-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, no advisory covering Blk 55 Lengkok Bahru in this window, and I do not assert the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route against it. That is correct, because the driver's dwell is a single unbroken 482-second run (derived.arrival.run_count = 1) — there are no separate in-geofence intervals to sum — so the absent advisory plays no part in the arithmetic and cannot trigger POL-NS-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02760-01", "EV-GPS-02760"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.run_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.60,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.60,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Ruling: DRIVER_COMPENSATION. The $4.50 no-show fee stands — the rider's claim is not supported — and the platform pays the driver $3.60 compensation. Why the fee stands. POL-NS-01 requires all four limbs and the record carries each. (a) EV-TRIP-02760 records the driver's 'arrived' event at 12:28:24. (b) EV-GPS-02760 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, with 49 qualifying in-radius fixes against the 3 consecutive fixes POL-NS-02 needs. (c) The in-geofence dwell runs from the first qualifying fix at 12:28:24 to the cancellation at 12:36:26 — 482 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null). The clock runs from the first qualifying fix, not the driver's tap (POL-NS-01(c)). (d) The driver terminated at 12:36:26 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. Nothing displaces that. POL-NS-03 does not apply: the stationary fixes are inside the radius (0 m from the pin), not outside it. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02760) holds one message and it is the driver's, sent 12:28:49 — the rider sent no locating message in the waiting window, so limb (a) fails. POL-NS-05 does not fire: the 'arrived' marker at 12:28:24 coincides with the first qualifying in-geofence fix (offset 0.0 s) at 0 km/h, so the marker is true. POL-NS-06 does not fire: a 482-second dwell is a 302-second surplus, not a shortfall. The rider's points. The rider says they were there, but their own device inside the same trace puts all 87 rider fixes 806–814 m from the pin, with rider_qualifying_fix_count 0 against the 100 m presence radius; the assertion is unsupported by the rider's own track and gives POL-NS-04 nothing. The rider also says arrival cannot be confirmed because no per-fix horizontal accuracy is shown. Rejected: the trace's computed facts already apply the POL-NS-02 filter and report 49 qualifying in-radius fixes; the geometry is given and is not recomputed, so the arrival test is affirmatively satisfied. The rider's fallback (POL-NS-02 → FULL_REFUND) therefore fails. Weight and confidence. EV-GPS-02760 is impaired: weight 0.85, issue GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW — a 60-second sampling gap (12:25:04–12:26:04) with 93.9% coverage. The gap is shorter than POL-NS-08(b)'s 120 s and lies before the waiting window, so it is not a policy-level impairment, does not engage POL-NS-09(e), and only down-weights the trace under POL-GEN-02. The deciding facts (in-geofence arrival and dwell) rest on EV-GPS-02760; the trip record's arrival and wait-timer events are the driver's own BUTTON tap, which POL-NS-12 says is not an independent carrier, and the driver's chat message merely repeats what the trace already shows. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.85 (POL-GEN-02(2)), above the 0.70 floor — the finding survives the discount and the case does not escalate. Payment. POL-NS-01 being satisfied in full and nothing from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80% of the $4.50 fee in force — $3.60 — the residual 20% being the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below the threshold of 4), so compensation is paid rather than withheld; on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at $3.60 (POL-GEN-03). The $3.60 effect is below the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05) and executes automatically. EV-FARE-02760's $4.50 cancellation-fee line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. No clause produces a referral on these facts. The missing advisory. EV-ADVIS-02760-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0) and can carry nothing; the driver's dwell is a single unbroken run, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation plays no part. Two claims about the advisory — one from each side — were discarded by the referee for citing a 0.0-weight artifact without naming its issue code."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

