    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a rider-filed dispute over the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02760. The fee stands and is not refunded; the driver is compensated SGD 3.60.\n\nPOL-NS-01 (read with POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05) holds on all four limbs. (a) EV-TRIP-02760 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 12:28:24. (b) EV-GPS-02760 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that time - 49 qualifying in-radius fixes at 10 s cadence, with the first in-geofence fix coinciding with the arrival marker (derived dwell_start_offset_sec = 0.0). (c) The continuous in-geofence dwell is 482 seconds, 12:28:24 to 12:36:26, against the 180-second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold applies). (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 12:36:26 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises, after the required dwell had elapsed.\n\nThe arrival marker is BUTTON, so POL-NS-12 does not apply (it covers only GPS_AUTO): the arrival and the dwell rest on EV-GPS-02760. That artifact is down-weighted to 0.85 on issue code GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW - a single 60-second sampling gap from 12:25:04 to 12:26:04, before the arrival and outside the waiting window, with coverage of 93.9 per cent. Under POL-NS-08(b) that gap is too short (60 s, against the 120 s threshold) and too early to be a policy-level impairment, so the trace is not impaired under POL-NS-08 and POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the ruling rests on that artifact and confidence is capped at 0.85, above the 0.70 floor. The finding survives the discount: the gap touches none of the 49 in-radius fixes and does not shorten the dwell run. I do not treat the driver's chat message 'hi im at the pickup point' (EV-CHAT-02760, sent 12:28:49) or the driver's statement 'Waited past the free period at the pin' as independent carriers - both merely restate what the trace already says, so neither lifts the 0.85 cap.\n\nThe rider's counter-arguments do not change the outcome. POL-NS-02's 25 m accuracy filter: no fix reports horizontal accuracy, and an accuracy-less fix is neither counted nor excluded by that filter, so the 49 derived qualifying fixes stand and arrival is established. POL-NS-03 is not engaged, because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius rather than outside it. POL-NS-05 finds nothing to correct (offset 0.0, held position, speed 0.0 kph). POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall: 482 s against 180 s is a 302 s surplus. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: the chat log holds only the driver's message, so limb (a) fails, and independently the rider track places the rider 806-814 m from the pin with rider_qualifying_fix_count = 0, far outside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius.\n\nThe fee therefore stands as it presently is (POL-GEN-03: NO_ACTION on the fee). EV-FARE-02760 shows cancellation_fee 4.50, matching platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 per cent of the SGD 4.50 fee - SGD 3.60 - the residual 20 per cent retained as the platform service fee; the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 1, below the required 4, so the absolute-count limb fails on its own). Because compensation is paid, POL-GEN-03 makes the emitted ruling DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60. The monetary effect is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically. No clause of this policy produces a referral on these facts. This ruling is provisional and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "EV-ADVIS-02760-01 is MISSING — no advisory covers the pickup in this window — so it keeps its identifier, has no payload, carries weight 0.0 and can corroborate nothing. Nothing in the bundle independently records conditions on the pickup road, and POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run in the driver's favour on a MISSING advisory. The driver's account that he waited 'past the free period at the pin' therefore stands on the single impaired trace and nothing else.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02760-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The missing traffic advisory costs this case nothing. EV-ADVIS-02760-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, no advisory covering Blk 55 Lengkok Bahru in this window, and I do not assert the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route against it. That is correct, because the driver's dwell is a single unbroken 482-second run (derived.arrival.run_count = 1) — there are no separate in-geofence intervals to sum — so the absent advisory plays no part in the arithmetic and cannot trigger POL-NS-09.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02760-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

