    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the $4.50 no-show cancellation fee stands and is not refunded. The driver arrived and waited as POL-NS-01 requires. EV-TRIP-02760 shows the 'I'm Here' tap at 12:28:24, the free-wait timer starting at 12:28:26, and the driver cancelling at 12:36:26 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. EV-GPS-02760 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (49 qualifying in-radius fixes, so the three-consecutive-fix test of POL-NS-02 is comfortably met) from 12:28:24, and shows him holding position there continuously for 482 seconds, against the 180-second free waiting period carried in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. Under POL-NS-01(c) that clock runs from the first in-geofence GPS fix, not from the tap (derived dwell_start_offset_sec = 0.0 s), and it exceeds the minimum by 302 seconds.\n\nYour arguments do not open an escape. (1) You say the arrival test cannot be confirmed because the trace reports no horizontal accuracy and the 49 qualifying fixes are a code assertion whose filter inputs are not before the judge. The qualifying-fix geometry is computed for this case and given in the brief; I do not recompute it, and the arrival test is met. (2) POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you: limb (a) fails, because the only chat message in EV-CHAT-02760 is the driver's ('hi im at the pickup point', 12:28:49), not a rider locating or coordinating message. (3) POL-NS-05 finds no false marker: the dwell begins within 0.0 s of the arrival tap and the in-geofence fixes record 0 km/h, far below the 15 km/h and 300 m triggers. (4) POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall: 482 s against 180 s is a surplus, not a deficit. (5) POL-NS-03 does not engage, because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it. Your own device track, at 806-814 m from the pin with 0 qualifying fixes inside the 100 m presence radius, is consistent with the no-show; I note it only for that.\n\nWhat remains of your case is the weight of the trace. EV-GPS-02760 is flagged IMPAIRED by the pre-pass at weight_multiplier 0.85, issue code GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW - a single 60.0 s sampling gap from 12:25:04 to 12:26:04, coverage 93.9%. Under POL-NS-08 that gap is shorter than the 120 s threshold and lies before the waiting window, so it does not impair the trace for policy purposes, does not engage POL-NS-09, and does not cap the outcome at PARTIAL_REFUND. The arrival and the dwell are decided on the trace, at the discounted weight.\n\nTo the driver: you are entitled to compensation of SGD 3.60, being 80% of the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in force (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd; EV-FARE-02760 derived money.driver_compensation = 3.60), the residual 20% being retained as the platform service fee. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check on EV-DPROF-02760 does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4 the first limb requires, so compensation is paid rather than withheld. Your account that you waited past the free period at the pin sits in the counterparty statement and supports the same finding; it carries no weight_multiplier and so enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence arithmetic.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact - in-geofence arrival and the length of the dwell - is carried by EV-GPS-02760 at weight 0.85. Neither the trip record's arrival and wait-timer events (a driver-pressed BUTTON marker, which POL-NS-12 expressly does not treat as an independent platform measurement) nor the driver's single chat message supplies that fact independently, so POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at 0.85, and not at the bundle mean. The finding survives the 15% discount because the discount arises from a short gap outside the arrival and dwell window that touches neither the arrival nor the measured run. EV-TRIP-02760, EV-FARE-02760, EV-RPROF-02760 and EV-DPROF-02760 all sit at weight 1.0.\n\nAmount and routing: on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling the two money fields carry the same figure, so amount_sgd = driver_compensation_sgd = SGD 3.60 (POL-GEN-03). The rider's $4.50 fee itself stands, which is the NO_ACTION disposition of the fee that POL-NS-07 describes. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so the ruling executes automatically. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
